digraph girls1foursLymeOldLyme {LymeOldLyme [URL="girls1foursLymeOldLyme.html"];Hopkins [URL="girls1foursHopkins.html"];GreenwichCountryDay [URL="girls1foursGreenwichCountryDay.html"];GreenwichCountryDay -> LymeOldLyme[label="18.7
04/11", weight="82", tooltip="NEIRA Boys & Girls Fours,Greenwich Country day, Hopkins, Lyme/Old Lyme			
Distance: 1500 Conditions: 7-15MPH cross tail to tail wind, higher gusts throughout the course. The starting line had the calmest wind to allow for good line ups. Comments: in the B4V4 Race Hopkins 2nd seat had a foot stretcher breakage at the 500m mark, they fixed it on water and continued to race. B5V4 was a novice race. G2V4 has Hopkins V3 race. G4V4 was composed of Hopkins v4, and v5 and LOL GN4. 
It was a sunny but windy day out on rogers lake. Although it was windy that made for some fast times for all those who went out! Lyme Old Lyme would like to thank the coaches and athletes of GCD and HOP for coming to our lake and racing with us. We hope to see you both at the NEIRA championships and with better conditions.
